  "limits": [
    "A toy with four qubits. Bayes' rule answers both questions by hand, and that is the reference. No speedup is claimed, and none is possible at this size.",
    "The cells are dark or bright. No photon counts, no blur, no resist chemistry, no mask, no wafer. Nothing here describes a real scanner.",
    "Rewinding runs a MODEL inside a quantum computer. It cannot rewind a real exposure.",
    "With the model's own check bit used as a filter, plain sampling's answers come back close to the rewound ones in this toy. What rewinding then adds on hardware is records per shot, not a different answer.",
    "A model worth asking this way is one too large to compute classically. The repository's 49-cell lithography circuit needs 389 qubits and, as built, up to about 3.4 million two-qubit gates per round; this job's largest toy circuit has 15. Closing that gap needs many qubits with far lower error rates, most likely error-corrected ones. That hardware does not exist today.",
    "One job on one device. The intervals are shot noise only."
  ]
